. A curmudgeon of an old man attached himself to Sazara upon graduation from primary, too stubborn to take no for an answer. For months the two traveled, as his sister began looking for eligible spouses for him. The curmudgeon hounded his steps, never friendly, but always there. As he visited the grave of his earliest friends, cut down by the plague, he saw the ghost of a child crying , and understood his connection. The old man nodded, &quot;About time kid. Lets get you some friends that'll last.&quot; And the old sidereal whisked the young Joybringer to Yu-Shan.<br /> Where he continued to be a morose wet blanket who liked talking to the dead. As often found at the Violet Bier as the Cerulean Lute, he is perhaps the best necromancer in the bureau of destiny, outside the Green Lady. His certainly is one of the creepiest, keeping a collection of ghosts in a Salon of Siblings made up of some of the Realm's house founders, including Peleps, Jyxall, Ledaal, Cynis, and Iselsi. More secrets of the realm exist in in that room than in the whole of the All-Seeing Eye. Of course, getting those ghosts to spill such a secret is an entirely different matter, and Sazara forfends any thought of harm to his brothers and sisters.<br /> Sazara watches the impending realm civil war with disappointment, wishing his sister's house could have done better. <br /> He has mastered Water Dragon style and Prismatic Arrangement of Creation, and is improving his skills in shadow throne style. The majority of his improvement is focused on researching more necromancy.<br /> Hooks- Any party to the realm civil war would give a favored daughter to have just 15 minutes in the Salon of the Siblings, and perhaps such an offer has been made. Why are the PCs offered to this mysterious old dragonblood they've never heard of and who doesn't show on any family registers to do some bizarre favor for, and why is their mentor making goodbyes?<br /> While the green lady and the rest of the Oracles are subtly displeased to have so many secrets not locked away, the idea of a dour Joybringer blocking them gives many useful tasks for junior Oracles to poke and prod at the necromancer's abode while he is distracted. <br /> attempting to befriend Sazara is a trial that none have truly accomplished, even with arcane fate. He seems cursed to solitude; but perhaps you could befriend this font of knowedge?<br /> Once a decade, the children of the Scarlet Empress gather together, both living and dead, to discuss their mother and recount stories of their youths. This weeklong festival has always been kept extremely quiet, lest she find out, but this is the first time she isn't around. And such a party needs someone to provide security and catering and all the other things that keep such an event going, so what are you doing there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4959-drdog","name":"DrDog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}